I walk to the front of the shop.
There are many things there.
I see a large white cotton scarf.
It is a very beautiful scarf.
That cotton scarf is very soft.
I take that scarf in my hand.
A clerk is standing there.
I look at him.
"What is the price of this scarf?" I ask.
"It is one hundred rupees, madam," he says.
One hundred rupees is a small price.
There is strong sun in Kochi now.
I go to the office by bus.
I can wear this scarf when going to the office.
This large scarf is good for blocking the sun.
"I am buying this," I tell him.
He nods happily.
